Java is both compile and runtime language

Reason:
java is both compile as well as run time.
when Main.src is converted into Main.class by compiler
Main.class is converted to byte code by interpretor

Java is pass by value

Reason:
when argument passed as primitive data types then copy of parameters is passed
and in case of non primitive data types like array or objects then copy of reference is passed
and that why if changes occur in object content also reflect in origional reference 
(both variables pointing to sama object).
